## 3. The 5 Quality Commandments for Building This Project

To ensure the codebase is clean, maintainable, and impressive to academic evaluators:

| Principle | Rule | Why It Matters |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **1. Contract-First** | Define TypeScript interfaces *before* writing UI or backend code. | Guarantees frontend and backend never fall out of sync. |
| **2. Modular Isolation** | Separate database logic, AI prompts, IPC handlers, and React UI into dedicated directories. | Prevents monolithic files that break when edited. |
| **3. Fail-Loud Logging** | Never write empty `catch` blocks. All database errors must be piped to the UI log viewer. | Makes debugging instant and transparent. |
| **4. Step-by-Step Verification** | Build and test Phase 1 before starting Phase 2. Run real database tests at each milestone. | Guarantees zero cumulative bugs. |
| **5. Defense-in-Depth AI** | Validate all AI JSON responses against a Zod / Joi schema validator before using them. | Prevents invalid SQL syntax from reaching the database. |
